description:
Design a frequency divider circuit that takes an input clock signal and generates an output clock signal with a reduced frequency. The division factor is configurable through a parameter, and the module includes a reset input to initialize the output clock and counter. On each positive edge of the input clock, the counter increments until it reaches a defined limit, at which point it toggles the output clock signal and resets the counter, thereby producing an output clock that is the original clock frequency divided by the specified factor.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg clk_div
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg clk_div
);parameter div_factor = 2;

reg [31:0] count = 0;

always @(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
  if (rst) begin
    clk_div <= 0;
    count <= 0;
  end else begin
    count <= count + 1;
    if (count == (div_factor - 1)) begin
      clk_div <= ~clk_div;
      count <= 0;
    end
  end
end

endmodule

