Design a 7-segment display decoder for a 3-bit wide input. The module takes a 3-bit input (A) and converts it into the corresponding 7-segment display encoding for numerical representation (0 to 7). The output is registered and synchronized to a clock signal, ensuring stable display updates. The design includes two pipeline registers to latch the segment data before presenting it on the output, providing a reliable and flicker-free output to the display.
