Design a binary-to-decimal converter that takes a 4-bit binary input and outputs a 3-bit decimal representation. For every 4-bit binary value from 0 to 9, the module will produce the corresponding decimal value from 0 to 9. For any binary input greater than 9, an invalid output of 3'd999 will be assigned. This module is useful in applications where binary values need to be displayed or processed as decimal numbers.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] bin,
    output reg [3:0] dec // Change output width to 4 bits to accommodate the range 0-9.
);

