Design a block that computes the Hilbert transform for a given input signal. The module takes a single input and produces two outputs: one representing the real part and the other representing the imaginary part of the Hilbert transform calculation. The real part is computed using the cosine of π/2 multiplied by the input, while the imaginary part is derived from the sine of π/2 multiplied by the same input. This module is useful in digital signal processing applications where phase-shifting and analytic signal generation are required.
module top_module(
  input signed [15:0] in,
  output signed [15:0] out1,
  output signed [15:0] out2
);

