description:
Design a glitch filter module that processes a digital input signal over a specified number of clock cycles to smooth out transient noise. It utilizes a shift register to store previous input values and calculates their average. When the incoming signal is within a defined threshold of this average, the signal is passed to the output; otherwise, it is filtered out. This effectively reduces the impact of short-duration glitches on the input signal, thereby providing a cleaner output signal for further processing.
module top_module(
  input signal_in,
  input clk,
  output reg signal_out // Change to reg since we are assigning in an always block
);

