description:
Design a circuit that functions as a data storage cell with control signals. On a rising clock edge, if the reset signal is not asserted, the cell stores an 8-bit input word when it is not yet valid, and subsequently outputs either the stored data or the input word based on the validity state. If the output is valid, the stored data is presented; otherwise, the original word is passed through to the output. This effectively creates a conditional data register that can hold and control access to temporary data.
module top_module(
    clk, rst,
    data_out,
    word,
);

code:
module top_module(
    clk, rst,
    data_out,
    word,
);input clk, rst;
    input [7:0] word;
    output [7:0] data_out;

    reg valid;
    reg [7:0] data;
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (rst) begin
            valid <= 0;
        end
        else begin
            if (!valid) begin
                data <= word;
                valid <= 1;
            end
        end
    end

    wire [7:0] data_out;
    assign data_out = valid ? data : word;endmodule

